==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{rfscript|Greek}} Greek '''ataxiā''' meaning "disorder", derived from '''ataktós''' meaning "disorderly"

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{pathology}} Lack of [[coordination]] while performing [[voluntary]] [[movements]], which may appear to be [[clumsiness]], [[inaccuracy]], or [[instability]].

====Synonyms====
* [[ataxy]]
* [[dystaxia]]

====Derived terms====
* [[ataxic]]

